From: bitbonsai <44185+bitbonsai@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Reveal hidden sidebar through window-local hover

Optional MA-007.c-hover candidate, not native runtime acceptance.
Baseline: Chromium 3e117efa80cec1c4e1e6fbfdf44edeb087a279a5 with
0002/0004/0005/corrected-0006/0007/0008/0009/0010 and normalized
0011, plus canonical 16-file foundation payload from fd3880d.
0012 is independent and is not required. Full index hashes below identify
all five exact input files, including independent endpoint rounding.

Observe only this browser window without adding a page hit target. Reuse
the native velocity heuristic, hover locks, animation/reversal and reduced
motion. Hover width uses the saved expanded width in the existing overlay
layout; persistent width continues through the existing toggle path.

Native interactive regression included but UNRUN. Real-header syntax and
scratch GN generation/header graph checks do not establish visual parity.
See browser/experiments/native-sidebar-hover.md in the myarc repository.

